id: pm-08mt4k
title: "pm next recommends outcome-milestone gates as actionable work, and summary.containers counts a bucket the envelope never emits"
description: "The single pm next recommendation is currently pm-w7ccmv, an outcome milestone with zero children that no agent lane can execute, and Milestones also appear in ready[]; separately summary.containers reports 27 with no corresponding envelope key. Both are the same root: item executability is not a declared dimension of the shared actionability definition, unlike the shipped decision_needed precedent."
type: Issue
status: open
priority: 1
tags[5]: agent-ux,"area:cli","area:sdk",context-management,relationships
created_at: "2026-07-25T17:53:10.100Z"
updated_at: "2026-07-26T05:57:31.991Z"
author: "harness:claude-code"
estimated_minutes: 240
acceptance_criteria: "Item executability is a declared, schema-driven dimension of the shared actionability definition rather than a per-type special case, so custom and extension-contributed types inherit it; gate-shaped items (outcome milestones and any type declared non-executable) never appear as pm next recommended or in ready[], and are surfaced in their own envelope bucket with a worklist exactly as decision_needed already is; summary.containers either gains a matching envelope key with rows or is removed, so no summary counter names a bucket that cannot be read; the held-out sets remain reachable through an explicit opt-in flag so no capability is lost; next, context, list-blocked and claim --next all consume the one definition and agree; a spec asserts that a workspace whose only unblocked items are gates returns no recommendation with an explanatory reason rather than recommending a gate"
parent: pm-mpbb
risk: medium
confidence: high
